WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:08.874
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:15.901
Unit twenty-five: Review: Skills for the Future. Today you will talk about future needs and abilities.

4
00:00:16.201 --> 00:00:18.900
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:22.983
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:24.689
Skill.

7
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:27.578
Skill means something you can do well.

8
00:00:28.183 --> 00:00:29.939
Coding is a useful skill.

9
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.924
Your turn. Say: Skill.

10
00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:36.594
Skill.

11
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:38.200
Future.

12
00:00:39.217 --> 00:00:41.228
Future means the time that will come.

13
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:43.619
The future belongs to learners.

14
00:00:44.217 --> 00:00:46.695
Your turn. Say: Future.

15
00:00:49.533 --> 00:00:50.395
Future.

16
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:52.116
Adapt.

17
00:00:53.117 --> 00:00:55.975
Adapt means to change to fit a new situation.

18
00:00:56.583 --> 00:00:58.618
We must adapt to new technology.

19
00:00:59.217 --> 00:01:01.788
Your turn. Say: Adapt.

20
00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:05.449
Adapt.

21
00:01:06.183 --> 00:01:07.405
Communication.

22
00:01:08.417 --> 00:01:11.124
Communication means sharing ideas clearly.

23
00:01:11.717 --> 00:01:14.575
Good communication builds strong teams.

24
00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:18.045
Your turn. Say: Communication.

25
00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:22.006
Communication.

26
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:23.832
Creativity.

27
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:27.141
Creativity means making new ideas.

28
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.993
Creativity helps us solve problems.

29
00:01:30.583 --> 00:01:33.630
Your turn. Say: Creativity.

30
00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.700
Creativity.

31
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.521
Critical thinking.

32
00:01:40.517 --> 00:01:43.886
Critical thinking means thinking carefully before you believe something.

33
00:01:44.483 --> 00:01:47.052
Critical thinking protects us from fake news.

34
00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.279
Your turn. Say: Critical thinking.

35
00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:54.471
Critical thinking.

36
00:01:55.217 --> 00:01:56.380
Technology.

37
00:01:57.383 --> 00:02:00.103
Technology means machines and digital tools.

38
00:02:00.717 --> 00:02:02.681
Technology changes every year.

39
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:06.214
Your turn. Say: Technology.

40
00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.300
Technology.

41
00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.399
Lifelong learning.

42
00:02:13.383 --> 00:02:15.975
Lifelong learning means learning all your life.

43
00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:18.989
Lifelong learning keeps your mind young.

44
00:02:19.583 --> 00:02:22.770
Your turn. Say: Lifelong learning.

45
00:02:25.633 --> 00:02:27.343
Lifelong learning.

46
00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:31.668
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:36.910
Visal, we've finished Book 1! Which future skill do you want to develop?

48
00:02:38.017 --> 00:02:41.447
Coding. After this course, I will be able to build an app.

49
00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.143
What will the future need?

50
00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:49.572
We will need to adapt to new technology, and we will need creativity.

51
00:02:50.683 --> 00:02:51.847
And your English?

52
00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:58.319
I will be able to communicate with confidence. Lifelong learning is my goal!

53
00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.118
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:01.983 --> 00:03:04.970
Grammar focus: Will need to and will be able to.

55
00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:06.538
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:08.890
We will need to adapt.

57
00:03:09.783 --> 00:03:11.237
I will be able to code.

58
00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:14.103
Students will need to think critically.

59
00:03:15.067 --> 00:03:18.961
Don't say 'will can'. Use 'will be able to' for future ability.

60
00:03:19.717 --> 00:03:22.857
Be careful! Don't say: We will need adapt.

61
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:27.009
Say: We will need to adapt.

62
00:03:27.309 --> 00:03:29.041
Say 'need to' + verb.

63
00:03:29.833 --> 00:03:32.323
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:34.448
Ready for Tomorrow.

65
00:03:34.748 --> 00:03:36.805
The future will need new skills.

66
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:41.506
Communication, creativity and critical thinking help us adapt.

67
00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:44.627
We will need to learn new technology.

68
00:03:45.633 --> 00:03:48.713
With practice, we will be able to solve new problems.

69
00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:52.280
Lifelong learning keeps us ready for change.

70
00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:57.310
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.824
I will be able blank code.

72
00:04:00.124 --> 00:04:03.058
A, to. B, can. C, will.

73
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.785
The answer is A: to.

74
00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.147
Learning all your life is blank learning.

75
00:04:12.447 --> 00:04:16.019
A, lifelong. B, future. C, critical.

76
00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:21.555
The answer is A: lifelong.

77
00:04:22.717 --> 00:04:24.496
Making new ideas is blank.

78
00:04:24.796 --> 00:04:29.053
A, creativity. B, communication. C, technology.

79
00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:34.867
The answer is A: creativity.

80
00:04:36.067 --> 00:04:39.137
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:39.983 --> 00:04:42.157
Which future skill do you want to develop?

82
00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:52.427
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:52.727 --> 00:05:04.133
I want to develop communication skills. In the future, I will need to work with people from many countries, and I will be able to speak English with confidence.

84
00:05:04.433 --> 00:05:06.166
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:11.409
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and will need to and will be able to.

86
00:05:11.709 --> 00:05:16.521
Today's value is adaptability. Be ready for rain or sun and change your plans.

87
00:05:16.821 --> 00:05:23.272
Congratulations! You have finished Online B two, Book one. See you in Online B two, Book two!

88
00:05:23.572 --> 00:05:26.434
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

